UPDATE public.flashcards SET cloze_text = $px$A cheerful person recalls happy memories more readily, and a sad person recalls unhappy ones — an effect called {{c1::mood-congruent memory}}.$px$ WHERE id = '088589fd-a5ca-4549-940a-c276bcb679c7';
UPDATE public.flashcards SET cloze_text = $px$The {{c1::visual cortex}} (sometimes called the striate {{c1::cortex}}) is located in the {{c2::occipital lobe}}. It performs the deepest analysis of {{c1::visual}} information — edge detection, color processing, motion analysis, and object recognition — drawing on input streams that have already been filtered by the retina, LGN, and other relays.$px$ WHERE id = '0950a42a-f46e-4029-9602-53cf9cc729af';
UPDATE public.flashcards SET cloze_text = $px${{c1::Subjective contours}} are perceived edges or shapes that have no physical counterpart in the stimulus. The classic example is the {{c2::Kanizsa triangle}}, where three notched circles create the illusion of a white triangle floating above them — the brain fills in contours that are not actually present.$px$ WHERE id = '09a74e95-3636-437b-aa7e-b02bef6d9d2f';
UPDATE public.flashcards SET cloze_text = $px$The {{c1::chalcogens}} (Group 6A) — oxygen, sulfur, selenium, tellurium, polonium — carry {{c2::six valence electrons}} and typically adopt a {{c3::−2}} oxidation state by gaining two electrons. Sulfur and the heavier members can also reach higher oxidation states (+4 in SO₂, +6 in SO₃ / SO₄²⁻) when bonded to more electronegative atoms.$px$ WHERE id = '0a7247dc-3575-4681-b553-d3cc156ac9c2';
UPDATE public.flashcards SET cloze_text = $px$The {{c1::Stereotype Content Model (SCM)}} classifies stereotypes along two dimensions: {{c2::warmth}} (intent — is the group a friend or competitor?) and {{c3::competence}} (ability to act on that intent).$px$ WHERE id = '0adc8674-3815-4acf-9b7a-ad12174880c7';
UPDATE public.flashcards SET cloze_text = $px$State functions of a system include {{c1::pressure, volume, temperature, density, internal energy, and entropy}} — each fixed by the current state alone.$px$ WHERE id = '0b184581-72d1-41f4-8972-93878b6b3be1';
UPDATE public.flashcards SET cloze_text = $px$A {{c1::conjugated protein}} carries a covalently attached non-amino-acid component — a {{c2::prosthetic group}} — that is essential to its function.$px$ WHERE id = '0b62af8b-afcd-470d-bda3-633cca68f5f8';
UPDATE public.flashcards SET cloze_text = $px${{c1::Correlation does not imply causation}} — to argue {{c1::causation}} from an observed {{c1::correlation}}, evaluate {{c2::Hill's criteria}} (temporality, dose-response, plausibility, etc.).$px$ WHERE id = '0bda2cb7-7ce9-4ca6-9165-6aafe4d6de60';
UPDATE public.flashcards SET cloze_text = $px${{c1::Partitioning}} describes how each compound divides between the two phases — those with greater affinity for the {{c2::mobile phase}} travel {{c3::faster}} and separate out earlier.$px$ WHERE id = '0c026c28-bbad-47b5-8d49-15054fee7d90';
UPDATE public.flashcards SET cloze_text = $px$The {{c1::atomic number}} (Z) of an atom equals the number of {{c2::protons}} in its nucleus and is what {{c3::defines the element}} — change Z and you change which element you have.$px$ WHERE id = '0c0736bc-c0df-47e8-8fb5-f0aeccc65992';
UPDATE public.flashcards SET cloze_text = $px$The {{c1::area under each NMR peak}} (called the integration) is proportional to the {{c2::number of protons}} producing that peak — used to count protons of each type.$px$ WHERE id = '0cda3ac9-bc3c-4195-8b07-93a01fac07a3';
UPDATE public.flashcards SET cloze_text = $px$Stability is measured by {{c1::binding energy per nucleon}}, which peaks near {{c2::iron-56}} — this is why both fusion of small nuclei and {{c3::fission of large nuclei}} release energy.$px$ WHERE id = '0ce3039f-3997-4bf1-b222-51f5f8956628';
UPDATE public.flashcards SET cloze_text = $px$At room temperature, the halogens span all three condensed phases: {{c1::F₂ and Cl₂ are gases}}, {{c2::Br₂ is a liquid}}, and {{c3::I₂ is a solid}} — the trend reflects rising molecular weight (and London dispersion forces) down the group.$px$ WHERE id = '0d84d208-3afe-4030-aa2d-c014c9545d08';
