UPDATE public.flashcards SET cloze_text = $px$When PaCO₂ climbs, dissolved CO₂ crosses the blood-brain barrier and lowers CSF pH; {{c1::central chemoreceptors}} in the medulla actually track this {{c2::H⁺ (falling pH)}} rather than CO₂ itself, and drive the respiratory center to {{c3::increase}} rate and depth — venting CO₂ until blood levels fall back to baseline (negative feedback).$px$ WHERE id = '44d0f367-219d-40c6-89b7-61e135c98202';
UPDATE public.flashcards SET cloze_text = $px${{c1::Lesion studies}} infer the function of a brain region by observing what behavioral capacity is lost when that region is damaged. In humans, naturally occurring {{c1::lesions}} (from stroke, tumor, or injury) are observed; in animals, {{c1::lesions}} can be created experimentally — most precisely using {{c2::stereotactic instruments}} that target specific regions in three-dimensional coordinates.$px$ WHERE id = '454ea1cc-1cb3-4aee-8050-1ce994536dae';
