UPDATE public.flashcards SET cloze_text = $px${{c1::Top-down (conceptually-driven)}} processing constructs perceptions starting from {{c2::memory and expectations}}, then fitting incoming sensory data into the predicted whole. It is {{c3::faster but more error-prone}} — perceptual illusions and misperceptions arise when the {{c2::expectations}} are wrong.$px$ WHERE id = '4a87a6db-f332-4617-9fd1-cdeca5f20426';
UPDATE public.flashcards SET cloze_text = $px${{c1::Pierre Flourens}} was the first to systematically study the functions of major brain regions using {{c2::extirpation (ablation)}} — surgically removing parts of the brain in animals and observing the resulting behavioral deficits. His work supported {{c3::localization of function}}.$px$ WHERE id = '4b511d27-50a1-4dd7-bee9-14d4eafa8826';
