UPDATE public.flashcards SET cloze_text = $px${{c1::Prions}} are infectious proteins — not living organisms — that cause disease by inducing a normal cellular protein to refold from its native {{c2::α-helical}} conformation into a misfolded {{c2::β-pleated sheet}} form that aggregates and resists degradation.$px$ WHERE id = 'a625abbe-779c-4e80-a0f1-3aac741a53c1';
UPDATE public.flashcards SET cloze_text = $px$Olfactory signals travel via the olfactory nerves to the {{c1::olfactory bulb}}, then along the {{c2::olfactory tract}} to higher brain regions including the {{c3::limbic system}}. Crucially, olfactory signals are the only sensory modality that bypasses the {{c4::thalamus}} — explaining why smells so directly evoke emotion and memory.$px$ WHERE id = 'a64994b4-9133-4942-a7cd-0335fa781f3b';
UPDATE public.flashcards SET cloze_text = $px$The {{c1::Eustachian tube}} connects the middle ear to the nasal cavity, allowing air to flow between them. Its function is to {{c2::equalize pressure}} across the tympanic membrane — the reason ears pop during altitude changes.$px$ WHERE id = 'a74a8495-21b2-432a-be4e-a258bd76b48d';
UPDATE public.flashcards SET cloze_text = $px$Cortical regions are classified as either {{c1::projection}} or {{c2::association}} areas. {{c1::Projection}} areas perform rudimentary motor or sensory tasks — the primary motor cortex and the primary somatosensory cortex are classic examples. {{c2::Association}} areas integrate input from diverse regions to enable higher-order processing such as planning and decision-making. The systematic body-part organization of the motor cortex is visualized in the {{c3::motor homunculus}}.$px$ WHERE id = 'a773b598-4a42-45ab-896c-20de8519f664';
UPDATE public.flashcards SET cloze_text = $px$Sitting inferior and posterior to the thalamus, the {{c1::pineal}} gland secretes {{c2::melatonin}}, an amine hormone whose blood levels climb as light fades — entraining the body's {{c3::circadian rhythm}} and ushering in drowsiness.$px$ WHERE id = 'a821ebd5-fc5a-47bd-847e-352a11568397';
UPDATE public.flashcards SET cloze_text = $px${{c1::Formal charge}} = V – Nnonbonding – ½·Nbonding, where V is the atom's neutral valence electron count, Nnonbonding is its lone-pair electron count, and Nbonding is its shared electron count.$px$ WHERE id = 'a839b6a3-f19a-477a-8a9d-069edb7fa933';
UPDATE public.flashcards SET cloze_text = $px$Pain perception arises mainly from {{c1::nociceptor}} activation. The {{c2::gate theory of pain}} proposes a spinal-cord gating mechanism that can {{c3::amplify or suppress}} pain signals before they reach the brain — explaining why distraction, rubbing an injury, or psychological state can change perceived pain intensity from the same physical injury.$px$ WHERE id = 'a84491d8-2ba5-40b0-be05-adb56022ebf3';
UPDATE public.flashcards SET cloze_text = $px$The {{c1::work-energy theorem}} states that the net work done on an object by all forces equals its change in kinetic energy: {{c2::Wnet = ΔK = Kf − Ki}}. This holds regardless of which kinds of forces are involved — conservative or non-conservative.$px$ WHERE id = 'a86d4cf8-6921-4b45-b717-993179d19ada';
