UPDATE public.flashcards SET cloze_text = $px${{c1::Self-concept}} is the whole set of beliefs we hold about who we are — our present, past, and possible future selves.$px$ WHERE id = 'bb569e0e-fc5d-455e-b270-094f52a74fd0';
UPDATE public.flashcards SET cloze_text = $px$The α-carbon of an amino acid is a {{c1::chiral center (stereocenter)}} because it bears four different substituents — except in {{c2::glycine}}, where the R group is just a hydrogen.$px$ WHERE id = 'bb776d6c-91db-4eab-8679-acd9e56fee54';
UPDATE public.flashcards SET cloze_text = $px$The {{c1::macula}} is a small central region of the retina densely packed with {{c3::cones}}. At its center sits the {{c2::fovea}} — containing exclusively {{c3::cones}}, no rods — which provides the sharpest visual acuity in normal daylight viewing. When you look directly at something, you are projecting it onto the {{c2::fovea}}.$px$ WHERE id = 'bc14f848-1fdc-4f55-a359-24e6b0a43a51';
UPDATE public.flashcards SET cloze_text = $px$The {{c1::corpus callosum}} is a thick bundle of {{c2::myelinated axons}} connecting the two cerebral hemispheres. It allows the dominant and non-dominant hemispheres to share information continuously — analytic language content from one side, emotional and contextual nuance from the other.$px$ WHERE id = 'bc593187-fb4b-4d24-a615-60d9806243bf';
UPDATE public.flashcards SET cloze_text = $px${{c1::Leptin}} is secreted by {{c2::adipocytes}} (fat cells) and decreases appetite by suppressing orexin production — a satiety signal whose levels correlate with adipose mass.$px$ WHERE id = 'bce5b17b-3535-47a9-a9cf-d7adf0b90b7f';
UPDATE public.flashcards SET cloze_text = $px$Carboxylic acids are excellent hydrogen bonders because both the {{c1::hydroxyl OH}} and the {{c2::carbonyl oxygen}} participate — the molecule is both a strong H-bond {{c3::donor}} and {{c4::acceptor}}.$px$ WHERE id = 'bdeff1a8-3cf4-45ef-a491-64843c902c43';
UPDATE public.flashcards SET cloze_text = $px$The {{c1::halogens}} (Group 7A) carry {{c2::seven valence electrons}} and need to gain just one more to complete an octet — which is why they have the {{c3::highest electron affinities}} of any group and are the most reactive nonmetals.$px$ WHERE id = 'be1a9ae7-9b98-46a7-ae11-0878027f83b0';
UPDATE public.flashcards SET cloze_text = $px$The cycle's hormone logic in one line: negative feedback dominates until estrogen peaks late in the follicular phase, briefly flipping to {{c1::positive feedback}} (the LH surge → ovulation), then reverting to negative feedback during the luteal phase, and finally being removed entirely when the corpus luteum degenerates — letting the next cycle start.$px$ WHERE id = 'beb2dabc-1436-4bce-9319-333f2823ef0e';
UPDATE public.flashcards SET cloze_text = $px$Dividing powers with the same base: {{c1::subtract}} the exponents — Xᴬ / Xᴮ = {{c2::X⁽ᴬ⁻ᴮ⁾}}.$px$ WHERE id = 'beea28c9-2cb5-4ee4-80d5-b82e3925c743';
UPDATE public.flashcards SET cloze_text = $px${{c1::In-group bias}} — viewing members of one's own group {{c2::more favorably}}; {{c1::out-group bias}} — viewing those outside one's group {{c2::more harshly}}.$px$ WHERE id = 'c109afdd-5b05-4332-b577-e236bb8f0169';
UPDATE public.flashcards SET cloze_text = $px${{c1::CETP (cholesteryl ester transfer protein)}} {{c1::transfers cholesteryl esters}} from HDL to other lipoproteins like IDL — converting IDL into {{c2::LDL}} in the process.$px$ WHERE id = 'c169a43b-a39a-4730-b4f4-9a6e93201213';
UPDATE public.flashcards SET cloze_text = $px$During brain surgery, a surgeon can stimulate the cortex with a small electrode and observe the behavioral or perceptual response. By systematically mapping which sites produce which responses, neurosurgeons can construct a {{c1::cortical map}} — historically a major source of our knowledge about cortical localization.$px$ WHERE id = 'c1a36136-5b77-400a-a01b-011fad369802';
UPDATE public.flashcards SET cloze_text = $px${{c1::Language}} is the most highly developed cultural symbol system — spoken, written, or signed symbols regulated by {{c2::grammar and syntax}} — and it expands communication across both space and time.$px$ WHERE id = 'c1e4e59a-6d9a-495f-881b-95050f8ceba5';
UPDATE public.flashcards SET cloze_text = $px$A {{c1::protecting group}} is a bulky group temporarily attached to a reactive functional group to {{c2::prevent unwanted reactions}} during synthesis — e.g., {{c3::diols or tert-butyl ethers}} can protect aldehydes and ketones.$px$ WHERE id = 'c271a1d9-7ba7-46f8-8a73-34516ebefac8';
UPDATE public.flashcards SET cloze_text = $px${{c1::Carboxylic acids}} contain both a carbonyl AND a hydroxyl group on the same {{c2::terminal carbon}} (–COOH); they are named by replacing the parent alkane's -e with {{c3::-oic acid}}, with the carboxyl carbon always assigned to {{c4::position 1}}.$px$ WHERE id = 'c2eb6f37-2174-414e-8530-9b15782dd5cf';
UPDATE public.flashcards SET cloze_text = $px$A {{c1::balanced polymorphism}} is maintained by {{c1::heterozygote advantage}} — e.g., sickle-cell trait stays common because it confers malaria resistance.$px$ WHERE id = 'c31fd23c-6477-41d0-8c3f-6701e5d05a4a';
